From 6bc7e105d609ef2a9b15c7e622106faecb95c1a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lance-index-build <lance-index-build@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:34:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(linalg): make the SVE f32 L2/dot kernels opt-in
 (LANCE_F32_SVE=1)

Default dispatch on aarch64 again selects the 16-lane scalar f32 L2 and
dot kernels, which the blocked flat-search kernels reproduce bit for bit
(vector::flat::pairwise::test_f32_rows_bit_identical). The SVE kernels
fuse multiply-add and reduce in a vector-length-dependent order, so they
agree only to rounding; LANCE_F32_SVE=1 selects them for pair and batch
calls together. The accuracy proptests still cover the SVE candidates.
---
 .../lance-index-bench/src/bin/assign_micro.rs |  2 +
 rust/lance-linalg/src/distance.rs             | 19 +++++
 rust/lance-linalg/src/distance/dot.rs         | 64 ++++++++++++-----
 rust/lance-linalg/src/distance/l2.rs          | 72 ++++++++++++++-----
 4 files changed, 119 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

